horse.

00:00:41.319 --> 00:00:44.339
Let's defeat Trump first before we worry about
whether he'll leave office.

00:00:44.339 --> 00:00:49.019
That's the most important thing, because if
we focus too much on what will happen if Trump

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:51.899
refuses to leave office, Trump might get himself
reelected.

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:52.899
And we don't want that.

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:53.899
That's number one.

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:55.699
So just go vote number two.

00:00:55.699 --> 00:01:01.499
If Donald Trump loses in November, on January
21st, 2021, he will no longer be the president

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:02.499
of the United States.

00:01:02.499 --> 00:01:03.829
He just will not be the president.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:04.829
OK.

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:06.890
That's the way that it is written in the law.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.530
And I am not particularly worried about Donald
Trump successfully not turning over power

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.650
to Joe Biden.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:19.210
If he loses in November, I do believe Trump
will claim that it was rigged.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:27.230
I do believe that it is likely that many Trump
ists could be moved to get on the streets,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:32.310
possibly with guns, if Donald Trump convinces
them that it was rigged and that really Donald

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.310
Trump won.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:36.040
I believe all of that that could well happen.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.490
But Trump will leave because he will not be
the president anymore on January 21st.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.490
Now, I know that there are some hypotheses
floating around.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:52.300
Here's what Trump could do to prevent this
from going to Joe Biden in January, if indeed

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.810
